course: dictionary
lesson: 6961
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Pallet is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it, which are its context. «A forklift truck lifts pallets on two steel forks» tells you that a pallet is something a forklift can lift, so it must be a flat platform for goods.
explain: Now read the story clues. «The prisoner slept on a pallet of straw on the cold stone floor.» Here a pallet is a simple bed made of straw, not a platform for boxes. The words sleep, straw and floor are the clues that point to this meaning.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. A pallet for goods fits a lorry and a warehouse. A pallet for sleeping fits a prisoner's cell. If the meaning does not fit, try the next one.
fact: A pallet is a flat wooden or plastic platform that goods are stacked on.
fact: Pallets help forklift trucks lift and move goods in lorries and warehouses.
fact: In old stories, a pallet can be a simple straw bed or a thin mattress on the floor.
fact: A potter may use a flat wooden pallet as a tool, but this meaning is less common.
fact: People sometimes make garden furniture out of old pallets.
exercise: «A forklift truck lifts pallets on two steel forks.» What is a pallet in this sentence? | A small car | *A flat platform for stacking goods | A steel fork | A bed for sleeping
exercise: «The prisoner slept on a pallet of straw on the cold stone floor.» What is a pallet in this story? | A lorry for moving goods | A flat wooden tool used by potters | *A simple straw bed on the floor | A garden table
exercise: Sam built a bench in the garden from old pallets. What are the pallets in this sentence? | Stories about kings and castles | Forks on a forklift truck | Thin mattresses for sleeping | *Flat wooden platforms that can be reused to build things
test: «The potter smoothed the clay with a flat wooden pallet.» What does pallet mean here? | A straw bed on the floor | A garden chair | A forklift truck | *A flat wooden tool
test: «The workers loaded the boxes onto pallets before the lorry arrived.» What does pallet mean? | A wooden spoon | A pottery tool | *A flat platform for stacking goods | A thin mattress on the floor
exam: «A forklift truck lifts pallets, and people keep to the marked walkways near them.» Which meaning of pallet fits best? | A flat tool for pottery | A straw bed in an old story | *A flat platform for goods | A garden bench
